    "title": "One Set Down, One Note Moves",
    "summary": "Slide a C major grip onto strings 2-3-4 and exactly one note needs fixing — the middle one, a fret lower — in every inversion, including the one grip where all three notes land on the same fret.",
    "tags": ["triads", "chords", "fretboard"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "Take " },
        { "text": "x x x 5 5 3", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": " — C major, root position, on strings 1-2-3 — and slide it straight down one set, frets unchanged: "
        },
        { "text": "x x 5 5 3 x", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": ". Same fingers, same frets, one string over. It sounds wrong, and it's worth hearing exactly why: low to high, that's "
        },
        { "text": "G3 C4 D4", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": ". There's a D in there. Whatever that chord is, it isn't C major."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Quick refresher, since it's been a chapter since the last one: "
        },
        { "text": "3·5", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " means string 3, fret 5. A chart is six slots, low E first, with an " },
        { "text": "x", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " for any string that isn't played, and string 1 is always the high " },
        { "text": "e", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here's the actual fix. On strings 2-3-4, the middle note of the grip sits one fret lower relative to the bass than it does on strings 1-2-3 — nothing else changes. The outer two notes land right where you'd expect; only the middle one needs the correction. That same one-fret adjustment works whether you're looking at root position, first inversion, or second inversion. Why the correction only shows up crossing onto strings 2-3-4 is coming later in this chapter — for now, just trust it and use it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Corrected for this set, the three grips fall in this order climbing the neck: first inversion down low, second inversion a few frets up, root position higher still. Start with first inversion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
